## Phase 1 — Patient 360 & Data Architecture
**Duration:** 2–3 weeks  
**Goal:** Build the **central structured context layer** — Patient 360 — before any AI features. This is the foundation everything else builds on.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The documentation explicitly states: **"Patient 360 should be built before AI features."** Do not skip ahead to AI integration until this is solid and tested.

### Domain Model (from UML Class Diagram)
Build all entities and their relationships:

```
User (userId, email, status, createdAt)
  └── PatientProfile (patientId, dateOfBirth, sex, bloodGroup, preferences)
        ├── MedicalCondition (conditionId, name, status, onsetDate)
        ├── Allergy (allergyId, substance, reaction, severity)
        ├── Medication (medicationId, name, dose, frequency, status)
        ├── Encounter (encounterId, riskLevel, intent, startedAt, endedAt)
        │     ├── Conversation (conversationId, createdAt)
        │     │     └── Message (messageId, role, content, createdAt)
        │     ├── ToolCall (toolCallId, toolName, arguments, result, status)
        │     └── ModelRun (runId, modelName, modelVersion, latencyMs)
        ├── LabResult (labId, testName, value, unit, observedAt, sourceId)
        ├── HealthDocument (documentId, type, storageUri, extractionStatus)
        ├── HealthEvent (eventId, eventType, eventTime, summary, sourceId)
        ├── WearableReading (readingId, metric, value, unit, recordedAt)
        ├── WearableTrend (trendId, metric, direction, baseline, computedAt)
        └── Provenance (sourceId, sourceType, sourceDate, confidence)
```

### What We're Building

**Database Schema:**
- All tables from the UML domain class diagram above
- Foreign key constraints and indexes
- Soft-delete support on clinical records
- Provenance as append-only (no destructive updates to sourced facts)

**API Endpoints:**
```
POST   /patients                     – Create patient profile
GET    /patients/{id}                – Get Patient 360 (scoped by consent)
PUT    /patients/{id}/profile        – Update demographics
GET    /patients/{id}/conditions     – Medical conditions
POST   /patients/{id}/conditions     – Add condition
GET    /patients/{id}/medications    – Current medications
POST   /patients/{id}/medications    – Add medication
GET    /patients/{id}/allergies      – Allergy profile
POST   /patients/{id}/allergies      – Add allergy
GET    /patients/{id}/labs           – Lab history
GET    /patients/{id}/timeline       – Medical timeline (HealthEvents)
GET    /patients/{id}/encounters     – Past encounters
```

**Medical Timeline:**
- Every clinically meaningful event stored as a `HealthEvent`
- Event types: `diagnosis`, `symptom`, `lab_result`, `medication_start`, `medication_stop`, `prescription`, `doctor_visit`, `surgery`, `hospitalization`, `vital`, `wearable_event`, `lifestyle_event`, `allergy`

