## Phase 2 — Document Intelligence
**Duration:** 2–3 weeks  
**Goal:** Convert uploaded prescriptions, lab reports, discharge summaries, and imaging reports into **structured, sourced, provenance-backed facts** in the Patient 360.

### Pipeline (from Document Upload & Extraction Sequence Diagram)
```
Upload → Virus/Malware Scan → Document Classification → OCR/Layout Extraction
→ Medical Entity Extraction → Normalization → Confidence Scoring
   ├── HIGH confidence   → Auto-write to Patient Record + Timeline Event
   ├── MEDIUM confidence → Request user confirmation/correction → Write confirmed record
   └── LOW confidence    → Flag for manual review / discard
→ Provenance ID saved (documentId, page, timestamp, model/version, confidence)
```

### What We're Building

**Document Service:**
- `POST /documents` — Authorized upload endpoint
- Malware/virus scan integration (ClamAV or cloud-native)
- Document classification model (prescription / lab / discharge summary / imaging)
- Object storage integration for raw file storage

**OCR / Layout Engine:**
- Integration with **Google Document AI** or **AWS Textract** or **Tesseract** (open-source fallback)
- Preserve layout structure for table-aware extraction (lab result tables)

**Medical Entity Extractor:**
- Extract: medications, dosages, diagnoses, lab values with units, dates, doctor names, facilities
- Implemented as a **Python microservice** (scispaCy + MedSpaCy / fine-tuned NER) exposed via REST
- Node.js Document Service calls the microservice over HTTP and maps results to `PatientProfile` fields
- Microservice is containerized separately — Node.js remains the primary API and orchestration layer

**Normalization & Confidence Engine:**
- Normalize medication names (→ RxNorm), conditions (→ ICD-10/SNOMED), lab tests (→ LOINC)
- Assign confidence scores per extracted field
- Three-tier gating: HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW

**Provenance Store:**
- Every extracted fact must record: `document_id`, `page`, `extraction_timestamp`, `model_version`, `confidence`
- Provenance is **append-only** — corrections create new records, not overwrites

**API Endpoints:**
```
POST   /documents                    – Upload document
GET    /documents/{id}/status        – Extraction status
GET    /documents/{id}/extracted     – Extracted fields (for user confirmation)
POST   /documents/{id}/confirm       – User confirms/corrects extracted fields
GET    /patients/{id}/documents      – Patient's document list
```

### Technology Stack
| Component | Technology |
|---|---|
| File Upload | `multer` (Express middleware) / `fastify-multipart` |
| OCR | Google Document AI / AWS Textract (`@aws-sdk/client-textract`) |
| Medical NLP / NER | **Python microservice** (scispaCy + MedSpaCy) — called via HTTP from Node.js |
| Normalization | RxNorm REST API, LOINC, ICD-10 lookups (HTTP clients) |
| File Storage | S3/MinIO (`@aws-sdk/client-s3`) |
| Malware Scan | ClamAV via `clamscan` npm / cloud virus scan API |
| Background Jobs | **BullMQ** (Redis-backed queue) — Node.js native |
| Queue Backend | Redis 7+ |
| File Types Supported | PDF, PNG, JPEG, TIFF |

### Deliverables
- [ ] Secure upload endpoint with malware scanning
- [ ] OCR pipeline producing structured text from PDF/image
- [ ] Medical entity extraction from structured text
- [ ] Three-tier confidence gating implemented
- [ ] User confirmation UI for MEDIUM-confidence extractions
- [ ] Provenance record created for every extracted fact
- [ ] Integration test: upload a mock lab PDF → verify extracted HbA1c value appears in `LabResult`

### Acceptance Criteria
- Malware-infected file upload returns `400` without touching storage
- OCR output from a sample prescription correctly identifies ≥80% of medication names
- HIGH confidence extractions write to Patient Record automatically
- MEDIUM confidence extractions are held pending user confirmation
- Every written `LabResult` / `Medication` record has a linked `Provenance` entry
- `Provenance` table has no UPDATE or DELETE operations (append-only enforced)

