## Phase 3 — Medical LLM Integration & Fine-Tuning
**Duration:** 3–4 weeks  
**Goal:** Select, benchmark, fine-tune, and deploy the **Medical LLM** behind the Model Router. This is the principal change from a generic LLM approach.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The LLM is **not** the source of medical truth. It is a reasoning and communication component. Safety, drug validation, and patient data access remain in deterministic services. Do NOT give the LLM direct database access at any point.

### Candidate Models for Benchmarking
| Model | Parameters | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **MedGemma 4B-IT** | 4B | Google's medical-domain Gemma instruction-tuned |
| **MedAlpaca** | 7B | Stanford Alpaca fine-tuned on medical data |
| **BioMistral-7B** | 7B | Mistral-7B fine-tuned on PubMed/biomedical text |
| **MMed-Llama3** | 8B | Meta LLaMA3 fine-tuned on multilingual medical data |

### Benchmark Evaluation Matrix
Each candidate must be evaluated on:
- [ ] **Clinical grounding** — Does it answer only from supplied evidence?
- [ ] **Structured output** — Does it correctly format tool-call JSON?
- [ ] **Hallucination resistance** — Does it fabricate drug names, lab values, or diagnoses?
- [ ] **Tool use** — Does it correctly select and call approved tools?
- [ ] **Safety compliance** — Does it defer/refuse unsupported requests?
- [ ] **Latency** — P50/P95 response time under load
- [ ] **Memory footprint** — VRAM requirements at target quantization
- [ ] **Multilingual** (if in scope)

### Fine-Tuning Pipeline (from Fine-tuning & Deployment Pipeline Diagram)
```
Collect permitted training/evaluation data
→ De-identify / quality review
→ Create task-specific datasets
→ Baseline candidate models
→ Fine-tune / instruction-tune
→ Run safety + grounding + tool-use evaluation
   ├── Meets model gate? YES → Package model + tokenizer + version
   └── NO → Revise dataset / training / candidate
→ Quantize if validated (INT4/INT8 via GPTQ/AWQ)
→ Deploy behind Model Router
→ Shadow / canary evaluation
→ Clinical + safety sign-off
→ Production
→ Continuous monitoring and re-evaluation
```

### What to Fine-Tune For
| Behavior | Description |
|---|---|
| Medical instruction following | Scope-appropriate response formatting |
| Grounded answering | Answer only from supplied patient/knowledge evidence |
| Structured tool selection | Correct tool name + JSON argument formatting |
| Adaptive symptom questioning | Ask ONE highest-priority question per turn |
| Source-aware explanation | Include source, date, uncertainty language |
| Refusal/defer behavior | Refuse unsupported requests gracefully |

### What Must NOT Be Delegated to Fine-Tuning
> [!CAUTION]
> These behaviors must remain in deterministic services, **never** in the LLM weights:
> - Emergency classification as sole safety mechanism
> - Drug-drug interaction truth
> - Patient-specific dosage calculation
> - Contraindication truth
> - Authorization, consent, or access control
> - Whether a proactive notification should be sent
> - Direct database access or unrestricted retrieval

### Model Architecture (Model Router)
```
User turn ──→ Model Router
                  ├── Primary Medical LLM (fine-tuned / adapted)
                  └── Specialist Model(s) [optional: extraction, multilingual]
                              ↓
                    Tool-Calling Policy
                              ↓
                    validated tool results
                              ↓
                    Response Safety Validator
```

### Tool-Calling Architecture (from documentation)
The LLM **requests** tools — it does not execute them. The Orchestrator validates and executes:

| Tool | Description |
|---|---|
| `get_patient_profile()` | Demographics, preferences |
| `get_medical_history()` | Conditions, diagnoses |
| `get_current_medications()` | Active medications |
| `get_allergies()` | Allergy profile |
| `get_recent_labs(test_name, limit)` | Lab results with timestamps |
| `get_wearable_summary(metric, days)` | Trend summaries (not raw readings) |
| `get_symptom_history(days)` | Prior symptom encounters |
| `get_relevant_documents(query)` | Matching health documents |
| `search_medical_knowledge(query)` | Medical RAG retrieval |
| `search_drug_information(drug_name)` | Authoritative drug facts |
| `check_drug_interactions(drugs[])` | Interaction lookup |
| `get_health_trends(metric)` | Derived trend signals |
| `get_clinical_guidelines(condition)` | Evidence-based guidelines |

### Deployment Components
| Component | Description |
|---|---|
| **Model Registry** | Versioned storage of model weights + tokenizer + eval metadata |
| **Model Router** | Routes turns to primary or specialist model based on intent |
| **Serving Runtime** | vLLM / TGI / Ollama (self-hosted) or Vertex AI endpoint |
| **Quantization** | GPTQ/AWQ INT4 for deployment size reduction |
| **Rollback Mechanism** | Blue-green or canary deployment with instant rollback |

### Technology Stack
| Component | Technology |
|---|---|
| Fine-tuning | HuggingFace PEFT (LoRA/QLoRA), Axolotl |
| Training Infrastructure | A100/H100 GPU (cloud: Vast.ai, RunPod, or GCP) |
| Serving | vLLM / HuggingFace TGI (Python-based — runs as a separate microservice) |
| **Node.js LLM Client** | `axios` / `node-fetch` — calls LLM serving runtime over HTTP/gRPC |
| Experiment Tracking | MLflow / Weights & Biases |
| Model Registry | MLflow Model Registry / HuggingFace Hub (private) |

