## Phase 7 — Clinical Safety, Escalation & Proactive Monitoring
**Duration:** 2 weeks

> [!WARNING]
> **Clinical Sign-off Required.** Escalation phrasing and notification thresholds must be approved by clinical advisor before patient-facing deployment.

**Goal:** Harden the safety boundary, implement human escalation workflow, and build the proactive health monitoring system.

### What We're Building

**Safety Engine (Full Implementation):**
- Independent of Medical LLM — deterministic keyword + ML-based pattern matching
- Gates BOTH input (pre-check) and output (via Response Safety Validator)
- Emergency scenarios: chest pain + dyspnea, stroke signs (FAST), severe bleeding, suicidal ideation, severe allergic reaction
- HIGH RISK path: skip ordinary AI pipeline → return pre-approved emergency response → log HIGH_RISK encounter

**Escalation Service:**
- Creates HIGH_RISK encounter records
- Queues encounter for human/clinical review
- Notifies emergency contacts (if configured by patient)
- Provides local emergency service information (by region)
- Human review dashboard for clinical reviewers

**Human/Clinical Review Dashboard:**
- Clinical reviewer role access
- Queue of HIGH_RISK encounters
- Ability to add clinical notes
- Ability to trigger follow-up actions

**Proactive Monitoring (Rules-Driven):**
- Trend analytics service analyzes wearable + lab trends → creates `HealthEvent`
- Versioned, clinician-reviewed rules engine determines if notification threshold is crossed
- LLM generates notification wording ONLY AFTER the notification decision has been made by rules
- Notification types: abnormal trend alert, medication reminder, appointment suggestion

### API Endpoints
```
GET    /escalations                  – Clinical reviewer: list HIGH_RISK encounters
PUT    /escalations/{id}/review      – Add clinical notes / resolve
GET    /patients/{id}/alerts         – Patient's active proactive alerts
POST   /monitoring/rules             – Admin: add/update monitoring rule
```

### Deliverables
- [ ] Safety Engine hardened with all emergency patterns
- [ ] Escalation Service creating HIGH_RISK encounters and notifying reviewers
- [ ] Human review dashboard (basic web UI)
- [ ] Proactive monitoring rules engine (separate from LLM)
- [ ] Notification generation gated by rules decision (LLM wording only)
- [ ] Clinical advisor sign-off on all escalation thresholds and phrasing
- [ ] Emergency response integration (local emergency numbers by region)

### Acceptance Criteria
- "I'm feeling suicidal" → emergency response returned within 200ms (no LLM pipeline delay)
- HIGH_RISK encounter appears in reviewer queue within 30 seconds
- Proactive notification for resting heart rate > threshold triggers rules check before LLM phrasing
- Emergency response cannot be customized or overridden by LLM output
- All escalations logged with timestamp, triggering pattern, model version skipped

