## Phase 8 — Wearable Intelligence, Advanced Personalization & Production Hardening
**Duration:** 3–4 weeks

> [!CAUTION]
> **Regulatory review may be required** depending on jurisdiction and wearable data usage scope. Consult legal and clinical advisors before patient-facing release.

**Goal:** Complete wearable integration, longitudinal recall, advanced personalization, and harden for production.

### Wearable Intelligence

**Key Rule from Documentation:**
> Raw wearable readings must NEVER be placed directly into an LLM prompt. Raw readings are normalized, quality-checked, and converted into rolling averages, baselines, and trend summaries — only derived signals enter clinical context.

**What We're Building:**
- Wearable data ingestion API (Apple Health, Google Fit, Fitbit, Garmin integrations)
- Data normalization and quality-check pipeline
- Rolling average + baseline computation
- Trend detection and `WearableTrend` record generation
- Trend summaries as the only wearable data exposed to LLM context

```
Raw Reading → Normalize → Quality Check → Compute Rolling Average
→ Detect Trend (rising/falling/stable) → Store WearableTrend
→ [If threshold crossed] → Proactive monitoring rules → Notification decision
```

### Advanced Personalization — Longitudinal Recall
- Facts stated once surface later when relevant via structured timeline retrieval (not by expanding model context)
- Conversation summarization: periodic summarization of older turns → store as structured `HealthEvent`
- Preference tracking in `PatientProfile.preferences`

### Production Hardening
- [ ] Load testing: 100 concurrent users, P95 < 3s end-to-end
- [ ] Chaos engineering: kill individual services, verify graceful degradation
- [ ] Model drift monitoring: weekly benchmark run, alert on safety metric regression
- [ ] Data retention / deletion pipeline (GDPR/HIPAA compliance)
- [ ] Disaster recovery runbook
- [ ] Incident response procedure documented
- [ ] Model rollback procedure tested (< 5 minute SLA)

### API Endpoints
```
POST   /wearables/sync              – Sync wearable data (batch)
GET    /patients/{id}/wearables     – Wearable readings (paginated)
GET    /patients/{id}/trends        – Computed trend summaries
```

