## Risks & Open Decisions

| # | Risk | Severity | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|
| R1 | Fine-tuned model fails to meet evaluation gate | HIGH | Plan for 2+ tuning iterations; maintain generic LLM fallback |
| R2 | Authoritative drug database costs / licensing | HIGH | Evaluate OpenFDA (free) vs DrugBank (paid); budget required |
| R3 | OCR quality poor on handwritten prescriptions | MEDIUM | Add human-review fallback for low-confidence extractions |
| R4 | Clinical sign-off delays blocking Phase 5/6/7 | HIGH | Engage clinical advisor in Phase 0; parallelize sign-off with development |
| R5 | Regulatory classification as medical device | CRITICAL | Legal review before Phase 5 patient-facing release |
| R6 | Model hallucination in grounded Q&A | HIGH | Response Safety Validator + hallucination test suite required |
| R7 | PHI exposure through LLM prompt logging | HIGH | Redact PHI from prompt logs; separate prompt audit from patient record |
| R8 | Wearable data quality issues | MEDIUM | Quality-check pipeline + confidence threshold before trend computation |
| R9 | Cross-user data leakage | CRITICAL | Enforce patient-scoped queries at DB level + integration tests |
| R10 | LLM context overflow with large patient history | MEDIUM | Context Engine enforces query-scoped retrieval; test with large Patient 360 |

